outputs.L1:
A (meth)acryloyl compound represented by the following formula (A), wherein:

- X represents a 2m-valent group having 1 to 60 carbon atoms or a single bond;
- each Z independently represents an oxygen atom, a sulfur atom, or no crosslink;
- each R¹ independently represents:
  - a linear, branched, or cyclic alkyl group having 1 to 30 carbon atoms;
  - an optionally substituted aryl group having 6 to 30 carbon atoms;
  - an optionally substituted alkenyl group having 2 to 30 carbon atoms;
  - an optionally substituted alkoxy group having 1 to 30 carbon atoms;
  - a halogen atom;
  - a nitro group;
  - an amino group;
  - a carboxylic acid group;
  - a thiol group;
  - a hydroxy group; or
  - a group in which the hydrogen atom of a hydroxy group is replaced by a vinylphenylmethyl group,

  wherein the alkyl, aryl, alkenyl, or alkoxy group may contain an ether bond, a ketone bond, or an ester bond;
- each R¹A independently represents a methyl group or a hydrogen atom;
- each k independently represents an integer from 0 to 2, provided that not all k moieties are simultaneously 0;
- m represents an integer from 1 to 3;
- each n independently represents an integer from 0 to 5; and
- each p independently represents 0 or 1.

